==Notes==
*Link Vitality can be equipped on [[Kubrow]]s, [[Kavat]]s, [[MOA (Companion)|MOAs]], and [[Hound (Companion)|Hounds]], but '''not''' on [[Sentinels]].
*Link Vitality cannot be equipped simultaneously with {{M|Enhanced Vitality}}.
*Link Vitality uses the player's maximum health as the base, which means using {{M|Umbral Vitality}} with the full set bonus, {{M|Primed Vigor}}, {{M|Gladiator Resolve}}, {{M|Saxum Carapace}}, {{M|Jugulus Carapace}}, {{M|Carnis Carapace}}, and {{M|Physique}} (with {{M|Coaction Drift}}) can further increase a companion's maximum health.
**Health buffs from other sources, including {{WF|Chroma}}'s {{A|Elemental Ward}}, {{WF|Wisp}}'s {{A|Reservoirs}}, or {{Arcane|Arcane Blessing}} also apply.
**With Link Vitality on a {{Companion|Sahasa Kubrow}} or {{Companion|Chesa Kubrow}}, a maximum health value of '''{{Math|((1+7.7+2.2+1.8+0.9+0.9+0.9+(0.18*1.3))*550+1725)*1.65+375*2}}''' can be achieved using the above health mods with an {{WF|Inaros Prime}}.

==Trivia==
*Prior to {{ver|34}}, this mod was named '''Link Health'''.

